[{:db/id 17592186119833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-70aeaa22-2b90-533e-ab1d-9dbd9f885f48" "question-53aad395-ec2e-5a47-9cdb-e404625e4482"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-70aeaa22-2b90-533e-ab1d-9dbd9f885f48" :question/id #uuid "70aeaa22-2b90-533e-ab1d-9dbd9f885f48" :question/math-academy-id "q-70807" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-1,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-2}{-1}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+1}{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-1,1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-1,2,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-1,2,1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ & =⟨1,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ & =-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z & =-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z+2 & =0 \\\\ x-2y-z-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b30e511f-0a3e-547f-96f1-0bfc53ad4766"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b30e511f-0a3e-547f-96f1-0bfc53ad4766" :answer-field/id #uuid "b30e511f-0a3e-547f-96f1-0bfc53ad4766" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25dcf144-1a51-5366-9800-5383c00b5a7d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aaf4ea99-1c7e-5b6b-af27-f81db06966e0" "answer-25dcf144-1a51-5366-9800-5383c00b5a7d" "answer-2b822cf8-78b8-5c6f-ba5e-a61ce1027e3a" "answer-08c0fd5d-eb30-51ed-9d57-ff0d86d1b905" "answer-b32a3885-cdf4-51dc-ad0e-0a3c46647043"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaf4ea99-1c7e-5b6b-af27-f81db06966e0" :answer/id #uuid "aaf4ea99-1c7e-5b6b-af27-f81db06966e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x-2y-z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25dcf144-1a51-5366-9800-5383c00b5a7d" :answer/id #uuid "25dcf144-1a51-5366-9800-5383c00b5a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y-z-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b822cf8-78b8-5c6f-ba5e-a61ce1027e3a" :answer/id #uuid "2b822cf8-78b8-5c6f-ba5e-a61ce1027e3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y-z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08c0fd5d-eb30-51ed-9d57-ff0d86d1b905" :answer/id #uuid "08c0fd5d-eb30-51ed-9d57-ff0d86d1b905" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y+z-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b32a3885-cdf4-51dc-ad0e-0a3c46647043" :answer/id #uuid "b32a3885-cdf4-51dc-ad0e-0a3c46647043" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y+z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119835 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e08b1f6c-36a3-5d41-8737-49d26e8563c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e08b1f6c-36a3-5d41-8737-49d26e8563c5" :question/id #uuid "e08b1f6c-36a3-5d41-8737-49d26e8563c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-128459" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(1,-2,0)$, $P(3,-4,1)$ and $Q(2,1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,-2,0⟩,\\,p=⟨3,-4,1⟩,$ and $q=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,1⟩-⟨1,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨2,1,-2⟩-⟨1,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+5j+8k \\\\  & =⟨1,5,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ & =⟨3,-4,1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ & =-9 \\\\ x+5y+8z & =-9 \\\\ x+5y+8z+9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34e50549-8287-5dd0-82ee-b77b6017695a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34e50549-8287-5dd0-82ee-b77b6017695a" :answer-field/id #uuid "34e50549-8287-5dd0-82ee-b77b6017695a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-102de1fa-9039-5418-a721-6fc419237fc4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-102de1fa-9039-5418-a721-6fc419237fc4" "answer-d6eccb3f-c3a2-58a8-b47e-683c853ab3af" "answer-c8ca9437-ca61-5c50-96e0-f167dfcd51fe" "answer-90536ec6-2590-5af2-a702-9be2e4b1ecdc" "answer-c7f81252-3be5-5daa-a718-63070020d187"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-102de1fa-9039-5418-a721-6fc419237fc4" :answer/id #uuid "102de1fa-9039-5418-a721-6fc419237fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5y+8z+9=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6eccb3f-c3a2-58a8-b47e-683c853ab3af" :answer/id #uuid "d6eccb3f-c3a2-58a8-b47e-683c853ab3af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5y+9z+15=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8ca9437-ca61-5c50-96e0-f167dfcd51fe" :answer/id #uuid "c8ca9437-ca61-5c50-96e0-f167dfcd51fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5y-8z+11=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90536ec6-2590-5af2-a702-9be2e4b1ecdc" :answer/id #uuid "90536ec6-2590-5af2-a702-9be2e4b1ecdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+8y+5z+6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7f81252-3be5-5daa-a718-63070020d187" :answer/id #uuid "c7f81252-3be5-5daa-a718-63070020d187" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5y+8z+7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-53aad395-ec2e-5a47-9cdb-e404625e4482" :question/id #uuid "53aad395-ec2e-5a47-9cdb-e404625e4482" :question/math-academy-id "q-330576" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(7,4,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-2}{4}=\\frac{z+1}{-2}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+4y\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨7,4,-3⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨5,4,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨5,4,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =⟨7,4,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z-57 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-51f6537d-feab-5ce3-9fc6-f89624d037a2" "answer-field-c79424ce-ee00-57d0-b195-b7db6dde7351" "answer-field-2f1bb041-bd3b-51ec-95b9-ab27a720aff3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51f6537d-feab-5ce3-9fc6-f89624d037a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "51f6537d-feab-5ce3-9fc6-f89624d037a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-fie